Python data types - 8 main types
-------------------------------

| # | Data Type   | Example              | Meaning                               |
| - | ----------- | -------------------- | ------------------------------------- |
| 1 | **int**     | `10`                 | Whole numbers                         |
| 2 | **float**   | `10.5`               | Decimal numbers                       |
| 3 | **complex** | `2 + 3j`             | Complex numbers                       |
| 4 | **str**     | `"Python"`           | Text/string                           |
| 5 | **list**    | `[10, 20, 30]`       | Ordered, changeable collection        |
| 6 | **tuple**   | `(10, 20, 30)`       | Ordered, unchangeable collection      |
| 7 | **set**     | `{10, 20, 30}`       | Unordered collection of unique values |
| 8 | **dict**    | `{'A': 10, 'B': 20}` | Key-value pairs                       |

=====

Also important

Python has a few other built-in types:

| Type       | Example         | Purpose             |
| ---------- | --------------- | ------------------- |
| `bool`     | `True`, `False` | True/False          |
| `NoneType` | `None`          | Represents no value |
| `range`    | `range(10)`     | Sequence of numbers |
| `bytes`    | `b'Hello'`      | Binary data         |


